# Memory-survival profile for the 1-GiB Prisma Compute instance class
# (OOM review, 2026-08-07). MEMORY knobs only — topology
# (INITIAL_SHARDS, FLEET_*) stays with each campaign's script.
#
# Every active deploy script sources this file and passes each line as
# --env; opting out requires UNSAFE_LEGACY_MEMORY_PROFILE=1
# explicitly. Values must be space-free (they are split into flags).
#
# A gather reserves min(capacity, max(ABSORB_GATHER_MAX_BYTES x3,
# worst-frame transient)); the binary floors the budget at the
# worst frame ((body ceiling + 64 KiB) x3 build multiplier ≈ 96 MiB at
# the 32 MiB pin). At this budget EVERY gather — not just oversized
# ones — runs ONE AT A TIME, so the slot count below is the effective
# truth. The startup summary prints the per-gather reservation, the
# configured slots, and the EFFECTIVE concurrency.
#
# DO NOT raise ABSORB_GLOBAL_GATHERS on a 1 GiB instance. An earlier
# version of this comment advised GATHERS=2 with a doubled budget; the
# 2026-08-09 chaos campaign ran GATHERS=4 in Singapore and the kernel
# OOM-killed the process (exit 137) roughly fifteen minutes in, while
# RSS was 362 MB against a 500 MB shed line and the reservations were
# accounted for exactly. The per-gather reservation UNDERSTATES the
# real transient of a concurrent gather; until that model is re-derived
# and validated, more slots trades a bounded, observable backlog for an
# unbounded fatal one. See docs/CHAOS-CAMPAIGN.md, CHAOS-5.
ABSORB_GATHER_MAX_BYTES=8388608
ABSORB_GLOBAL_BUDGET_BYTES=100859904
ABSORB_GLOBAL_GATHERS=1
SLATEDB_RT_THREADS=4
TELEMETRY_CACHE_BYTES=16777216
SHARED_CACHE_BYTES=134217728
HISTORY_CACHE_BYTES=33554432
POSTINGS_CACHE_BYTES=67108864
MAX_UNFLUSHED_BYTES=16777216
L0_SST_SIZE_BYTES=8388608
L0_MAX_SSTS=32
ADMIT_RSS_SHED_MB=500
